---
import Base from "@Layout/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	Title="Aphrodite - CCR compression proxy for Hermes Agent"
	Description="CCR compression proxy + absorptive preview pipeline for Hermes Agent. Up to 610x compression on the standard corpus (132x overall), ~10 ms end-to-end. One binary. Zero dependencies."
>
	<main class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-5xl flex-1 flex-col gap-16 px-6 py-16">
		<section class="flex flex-col gap-6">
			<h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">Aphrodite</h1>
			<p class="max-w-3xl text-lg text-neutral-600">
				CCR compression proxy + absorptive preview pipeline for Hermes Agent.
				Up to 610&times; compression on the standard corpus (132&times; overall),
				~10&nbsp;ms end-to-end, type-aware classifier, TOML-driven, opt-in config
				auto-reload.
			</p>
			<p class="text-lg font-medium">One binary. Zero dependencies. Millions of tokens saved.</p>
			<nav class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
				<a class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 px-4 py-2" href="/setup/"
					>Setup</a
				>
				<a class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 px-4 py-2" href="/crates/"
					>Crates</a
				>
				<a
					class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 px-4 py-2"
					href="/versions/"
					>Versions</a
				>
			</nav>
		</section>

		<section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The problem</h2>
			<p class="max-w-3xl text-neutral-600">
				Every file read, build, code search, or browser open floods the agent's context with
				raw output - compilation logs, accessibility trees, JSON blobs. The agent spends its
				budget reading noise instead of reasoning.
			</p>
			<p class="max-w-3xl text-neutral-600">
				Aphrodite intercepts output before it reaches the LLM and replaces it with a compact,
				structured preview. The agent sees ~15 tokens of metadata instead of hundreds - and
				retrieves the full content only when it actually needs it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The pipeline</h2>
			<ol class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-3 text-neutral-600">
				<li>
					<strong>1. Classify.</strong> A type-aware classifier names the content (build
					output, diff, JSON, browser snapshot...). Classification alone takes 40-123&nbsp;ns.
				</li>
				<li><strong>2. Preview.</strong> An enriched, type-aware preview is rendered.</li>
				<li>
					<strong>3. Store.</strong> Full content lands in CCR storage (BLAKE3, SQLite or
					in-memory) behind a
					<code class="font-mono text-sm">&lt;&lt;&lt;CCR:hash|type|size&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> marker.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>4. Decide.</strong> The agent retrieves only when needed, via
					<code class="font-mono text-sm">aphrodite_retrieve(hash)</code>.
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="max-w-3xl text-neutral-600">
				Aphrodite reaches the agent two ways: as a native Hermes plugin with hook-level
				interception (no API round-trip), or as a reverse proxy for any OpenAI-compatible
				client, compressing Chat Completions responses through CCR with a tool relay.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The numbers</h2>
			<table class="max-w-2xl text-sm">
				<thead>
					<tr class="border-b border-neutral-300 text-left">
						<th class="py-2 pr-6 font-medium">Content type</th>
						<th class="py-2 font-medium">Compression</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="text-neutral-600">
					<tr><td class="py-1.5 pr-6">Browser snapshot</td><td class="py-1.5">416&times;</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-1.5 pr-6">Build output</td><td class="py-1.5">140&times;</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-1.5 pr-6">JSON</td><td class="py-1.5">40&times;</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-1.5 pr-6">Git diff</td><td class="py-1.5">23&times;</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-1.5 pr-6">Terminal</td><td class="py-1.5">20&times;</td></tr>
					<tr class="border-t border-neutral-300">
						<td class="py-1.5 pr-6 font-medium text-neutral-900">Median</td>
						<td class="py-1.5 font-medium text-neutral-900">23&times; fewer tokens on tool output</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
			<p class="max-w-3xl text-sm text-neutral-600">
				Measured in the real world across 200 Hermes sessions (6,843 API calls,
				Sep&nbsp;18-20, 2026): 156,342,817 tokens saved of 581,302,405 expanded - 26.9%
				(the exact percentage is a band: ~24-33% across a 3.0-4.5 chars/token sensitivity
				range, centered ~27%). 183 of 200 sessions saved; tool-heavy workloads scale to
				20-25%, pure-tool to 76-82%.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Install</h2>
			<p class="max-w-3xl text-neutral-600">
				The recommended path is the Hermes plugin; the proxy binary also installs
				standalone via Cargo. Full instructions on the
				<a class="underline" href="/setup/">setup page</a>.
			</p>
			<pre
				class="max-w-3xl overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 p-4 font-mono text-sm"><code>git clone https://github.com/PlayForm/Aphrodite-Hermes.git
cd Aphrodite-Hermes
bash download.sh
hermes plugins enable aphrodite</code></pre>
		</section>
	</main>

	<footer class="border-t border-neutral-200 px-6 py-8 text-sm text-neutral-500">
		Aphrodite - CC0-1.0, public domain. Built by PlayForm.
	</footer>
</Base>
